{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.108562Z","id":"5820c9221d99f2ba90540d9569cb078db6551f7650dbeab74665eb27239cc3e9","body":{"detail":"Deferred by the owner (D5, line 31): version 1 keeps current identity systems; reporter tokens minted by the deployer's backend (§5.3) cover filing without a Clax identity.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"d57e8df1c79607b1e70dfc4ec2addbe90e02b723af407580d7b1af1e26d68141"},"summary":"Deployer-defined identity: OIDC sign-in and RFC 8693 token exchange against the deployer's IdP","supersedes":"395bca448814296a21c55a58c207dc4974216621af8851130cf5fadc5f2dcdf0","tags":["revisit:a deployer without a backend (a pure SPA) needs to mint reporter tokens","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.209455Z","id":"37ab530e5199d28179dbc2c937f9a3d4d8f2bcb6f6d5e93885c799d77a7f4bf6","body":{"detail":"Accepted for version 1: running it in Kubernetes is out of scope (D4), and one replica with a persistent volume is the supported shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"397d8aa0be732f8bdee5662903082203c70572dd00e73312b7102ff38628f5a1"},"summary":"A deployer's Clax runs as one replica: the store is SQLite with one writer","supersedes":"27e20e31cbd0a85f83f6278b33c3a069a38c8f92195d35df98bfcbb1b71b262c","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.312127Z","id":"d513ae48f63b046773b1d1348cd1233742b0150e6ada62a42e71505a7e814a35","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for opaque metadata Clax does not interpret (D6, line 33); a schema and an index are only needed once Clax filters by it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":442},"content_hash":"4660a2ab6bcfdb863d8dd3f20eda5f87cef2cf69bfe528e0b659cb140e638dd2"},"summary":"Registered sources with a JSON Schema for metadata, and queries over metadata","supersedes":"7c9e0e9f41418762d86bd419699adab5fc8c9052783e8420fb76fedf04c4a29d","tags":["revisit:an agent or app needs to list reports by a metadata field","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.416852Z","id":"3956282045cb7dd6b2113edaf1bb9ee22105b25dd793dd8e9215d3a62f8b351b","body":{"detail":"Not now: it needs a migration of the live-page tables, which installed databases have; external artifacts are a new kind beside live instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":443},"end":{"line":443},"content_hash":"1ba59b3f3f5075ec0d89d733f34a2b50e0305c59a45fbb75fed5640d62d84968"},"summary":"Make live pages external artifacts of a built-in web source, one model instead of two","supersedes":"15ff2f16280128d6701b7b90ee05a8e9053d07bb5a680f368138110ce0d64258","tags":["revisit:a fix has to be made twice, once for live pages and once for external artifacts","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.523912Z","id":"a86586e51ba37503694e82e5d84c6b8eb5baeb39f2d418a3c4a6abb3654e1765","body":{"detail":"Proposed in §5.1-§5.2; not yet accepted. Today the extension's credential is the owner identity (crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs), which cannot be right on a hosted Clax the extension must reach (D1).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"305d6308c9ffb2a9934fcdafecbb622e25f6c8d5ede4fdf24b202b97012353a9"},"summary":"Decide the credential model: browser session and signed grants only, consent only in a browser session, daemon token as a bootstrap, the extension's cxe_ credential replaced by a grant","supersedes":"283da5c7043b66639902fca475fb1aebf95ec9f2531f2f83a7d30e1551ff10aa","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.629550Z","id":"469ff1217f49422f29b9a0f4cfa46341982f946e4ed66d79ea7f6139fb960621","body":{"detail":"Per instance lets everyone on one organization's instance share an artifact by its external ID; on clax.dev an ID another person holds is then 409 external_id_taken to someone who may not read it. Per person never collides, but two colleagues get two artifacts for one record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"dda02cdf311ff69548e88c1cc59f58bfedbd2b32db88fe412023cebb4c9e6643"},"summary":"Decide the uniqueness scope of external_id: per instance (proposed) or per creating person","supersedes":"7817911aa2dde3311dc6d040e2b57778aea54ef671810c45e14c366c0edac1bd","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.734242Z","id":"0daa09552e4d5456d0408a92763056f8da60237b74065448ee8743bd99e366c1","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"92d117b022d6f61ff8b6829446a617637a40f4e3579a5302f41e5d830d747c60"},"summary":"Decide who may write an artifact's metadata: anyone who may edit it (proposed) or only its creator","supersedes":"392bbc7508a14791eefe0f07fc7483a1edfb3a364d067e29d1681c8612879689","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.839113Z","id":"bd228eda7de5697457c560ae565b35049087548135c08c2e265cee524aea6912","body":{"detail":"§6.1 and §6.4 read D6 this way; the owner stated the opaque identifier and metadata without naming what they attach to.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"fd28ced0a83952818697ca5e7d4de32a54114cd514293280e27cad305f3cce23"},"summary":"Confirm the opaque ID and metadata of D6 attach to both artifacts (external_id, metadata) and threads (reporter_id, metadata)","supersedes":"a908b6f897f8cdacf4c1a6600debba746d0c2c2f9ee41b68a8af25abc4fe44d1","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
